# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Homebrew's usage reports are off (DESIGN §9.3: no telemetry; #36).
# The nightly updater runs brew update and brew upgrade with no terminal,
# and the Homebrew copy in the image counts its notice about the reports
# as already shown. Without this line it would send them to
# analytics.brew.sh and nobody would see that it does. bin/brew reads
# this file itself, so the line reaches the updater's runs too.
#
# bin/brew then reads Homebrew's own brew.env and the owner's
# (~/.homebrew/brew.env, or under XDG_CONFIG_HOME), and a line there
# replaces one from here: an empty HOMEBREW_NO_ANALYTICS turns the
# reports back on. Homebrew belongs to uid 1000, who may not be a
# Guardian. HOMEBREW_SYSTEM_ENV_TAKES_PRIORITY makes bin/brew read this
# file again after those two, so this one wins.
#
# This is a default, not a lock. A Guardian's switch can change this file
# later, and bootc keeps a changed file in /etc across updates.
#
# bin/brew exports each line that starts with HOMEBREW_ exactly as it is
# written and skips every other line. So no quotes, and no comment after
# a value.
HOMEBREW_NO_ANALYTICS=1
HOMEBREW_SYSTEM_ENV_TAKES_PRIORITY=1
